# Template for the gitignored `.env`. Copy to `.env` and fill in locally.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# NEVER commit `.env`. The repository is public (github.com/ianshank/Orbital-Drift)
# and Constitution VII allows no credentials in it, ever. `.gitignore` excludes
# `.env`; `ci/gitleaks.toml` has a path rule as a backstop.
#
# Values here are host-specific by design (D-10): the repo stays parameterised so
# a public clone reveals nothing about node A's network or hardware. Terraform
# consumes the same values via `*.tfvars`, which are also gitignored — the
# `*.tfvars.example` templates arrive with T006-T010, which own those variables.
#
# Placeholders only below. Leave every value empty.

# --- Node A (the k3s host) ----------------------------------------------------
# LAN address and hostname of the single-node cluster. Used by runbooks and by
# any local tooling that talks to the cluster from the authoring machine.
NODE_A_LAN_IP=
NODE_A_HOSTNAME=

# --- GPU pinning (D-03) -------------------------------------------------------
# From `nvidia-smi -L` on node A. Include the `GPU-` prefix; UUIDs only — PCI bus
# IDs and indices are rejected by the JIT-CDI path / are not reboot-stable.
# These identify physical hardware and MUST NOT be committed.
#   ORBITAL_DRIFT_TRAIN_GPU_UUID   -> RTX 5060 Ti 16GB (training)
#   ORBITAL_DRIFT_SERVE_GPU_UUID   -> RTX 5060 8GB     (serving / aux)
ORBITAL_DRIFT_TRAIN_GPU_UUID=
ORBITAL_DRIFT_SERVE_GPU_UUID=
